Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: disable RTL8261x LED output when turning it off

rtl8261x_led_brightness_set() keeps the per-LED output enable (LCR7
EN) set for both brightness states and only drives the output level
low for LED_OFF.  With no link the PHY LED engine stays quiet and the
manual level holds (verified on an XR1710G lan2 with no cable), but on
an active link the PHY firmware LED engine keeps re-asserting the
speed mask and the LCR6 activity-blink bits: the "off" LED comes back
solid green and the "off" amber keeps blinking with traffic.

Clear EN together with the low level for LED_OFF so the output stage
is disabled outright; the firmware LED engine cannot light a LED whose
output is disabled.  LED_ON behaviour is unchanged.

Tested on Gemtek XR1710G (AN7581 + RTL8261BE): wan link stays up,
both jack LEDs follow LuCI None/off and stay dark; lan2 stays under
manual control as before.
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -2462,7 +2462,7 @@
 				       enum led_brightness value)
 {
 	struct rtl8261x_priv *priv = phydev->priv;
-	u16 lcr7 = RTL822X_VND2_LED_EN(index);
+	u16 lcr7 = value == LED_OFF ? 0 : RTL822X_VND2_LED_EN(index);
 	bool active_low, on;
 	int ret;
 
